  "solution": {
    "text": "Let  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>  be the normal reaction between  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>  and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> ,<br/><br/>Equilibrium of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> <br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>∘</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>     ... (i)<br/><br/>Equilibrium of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>  in vertical direction gives<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>∘</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>     ... (ii)<br/><br/>From Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
